<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RBM mode's gear of Commander Battle's Sturgian troop classes (cb_mpclassdivisions_sturgia.xml), read by
  CommanderBattle/RbmLoadouts.cs in place of the classes' mp_ gear when the host turns RBM mode on. Same rules as the
  class's own characters (cb_mpcharacters_sturgia.xml):
  - One Class per MPHeroClass id. Hero is the commander's gear; Troop holds the bots' rosters. Bots draw every slot
    from a random roster, so each slot holds the same kind of item in every roster: the rosters vary the looks (armour
    and helmets of one tier), never the loadout. Weapons, shield, horse and harness are the same in every roster.
  - Setup N replaces weapon setup perk N of the class (index 0 is the class's own loadout and has no entry). Each slot
    mirrors one AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn of the perk; no id empties the slot (two-handers clear the shield, axe
    setups and the two-handed axe clear the sidearm).
  - Slots: Item0 main weapon (or bow), Item1 shield (or arrows), Item2 sidearm (the levy's raider axe, the men-at-arms'
    northern sword, the riders' two-handed maul, the archers' two-handed axe), Cape shoulder pieces. Mounted classes
    carry a horse and harness in every roster; foot classes none.
  - Items only from the singleplayer and RBM item files that RBM.Multiplayer loads in multiplayer (no mp_ items, no
    looter or Nord items), mostly the ones RBM's troop overhaul (RBMCombat_unit_overhaul.xml) gives Sturgian troops,
    so they carry RBM's stats. Shields are the plain ids, not RBM's _shoulder copies: those use RBM's own holsters,
    which multiplayer doesn't load.
  - Doctrine: the shield-wall culture. The biggest round shields, the heaviest infantry armour; two-handed axe
    berserkers; cavalry with big round shields and two-handed maces. Weak ranged (composite short bows, plain
    arrows), no pikes, no throwing weapons.
  - Gear tiers: light = levy (leather tabards and padded coats, nasal helmets, the crude large round shield, a raider
    axe); medium = men-at-arms (hauberks and lamellar, goggled helmets, the iron-rimmed round shield, a long warsword);
    heavy = varyags and druzhina (lamellar, coats of plates, closed and lord's helmets, plated limbs, brass lamellar
    shoulders). The archers sit a step below the infantry of their weight.
  - Seeds (SP troop of the same role and tier in RBM's overhaul):
      levy spearman   sturgian_recruit, sturgian_warrior
      shield warrior  sturgian_spearman, sturgian_soldier
      varyag          sturgian_veteran_warrior (heavy axeman), sturgian_shock_troop; the axes sturgian_ulfhednar
      levy bowman     sturgian_militia_archer, sturgian_hunter
      veteran bowman  sturgian_veteran_bowman (bow, axe, helmets; lighter mail than RBM's, to stay below the infantry)
      horse raider    sturgian_warrior_son (son of boyar), varyag; lance and maul from druzhinnik / varyag_veteran
      druzhinnik      druzhinnik; heavy lance from druzhinnik_champion
      general         druzhinnik_champion
-->
